<h2 class="wp-block-heading">How Many Moving Boxes Do I Need?</h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Most homes need somewhere between 20 and 150 boxes, depending on the number of rooms and how much is in them. The moving supply guide at <a href="https://www.movingplace.com/moving-advice/how-many-moving-boxes-do-i-need" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Moving Place</a> gives these ranges for an average move, and our moving box calculator lands inside them for each home size:</p>



<figure class="wp-block-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Home size</th><th>Average move (Moving Place)</th><th>Our calculator, average stuff</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Studio</td><td>20–30 boxes</td><td>25 boxes</td></tr><tr><td>1-bedroom apartment</td><td>30–40 boxes</td><td>37 boxes</td></tr><tr><td>2-bedroom apartment</td><td>50–60 boxes</td><td>50 boxes</td></tr><tr><td>3-bedroom house</td><td>80–100 boxes</td><td>83 boxes</td></tr><tr><td>4-bedroom house</td><td>100–125 boxes</td><td>114 boxes</td></tr><tr><td>5+ bedroom house</td><td>130–160 boxes</td><td>136 boxes</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Light packers can need about a third fewer boxes, and homes with full closets, lots of books or a packed garage can need a third more. A quick rule from a packaging expert quoted by <a href="https://www.redfin.com/blog/2016/03/moving-soon-this-guide-will-help-you-figure-out-how-many-boxes-you-need.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Redfin</a> is 10 to 15 boxes per room, and the same article suggests buying about 10 percent more than your estimate, so a few spare boxes are always on hand for the last-minute items.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" width="1536" height="1024" src="https://dailyspacehacks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/moving-box-calculator-01-packed-boxes.jpg" alt="Moving box calculator: stacks of sealed cardboard moving boxes in several sizes and a wardrobe box with shirts on hangers in a bright living room on moving day" class="wp-image-2333" srcset="https://dailyspacehacks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/moving-box-calculator-01-packed-boxes.jpg 1536w, https://dailyspacehacks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/moving-box-calculator-01-packed-boxes-300x200.jpg 300w, https://dailyspacehacks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/moving-box-calculator-01-packed-boxes-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://dailyspacehacks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/moving-box-calculator-01-packed-boxes-768x512.jpg 768w" sizes="(max-width: 1536px) 100vw, 1536px" /></figure>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Moving Box Sizes and What to Pack in Each</h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The golden rule is simple: the heavier the item, the smaller the box. A large box full of books is too heavy to lift safely and can split, while a small box of pillows wastes space. These are typical sizes for standard US moving boxes:</p>



