<figure class="wp-block-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Box</th><th>Typical size</th><th>Volume</th><th>Best for</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Small</td><td>16 x 12 x 12 in (41 x 30 x 30 cm)</td><td>1.5 cu ft</td><td>Books, dishes, canned food, tools</td></tr><tr><td>Medium</td><td>18 x 18 x 16 in (46 x 46 x 41 cm)</td><td>3 cu ft</td><td>Kitchen items, toys, decor, shoes</td></tr><tr><td>Large</td><td>18 x 18 x 24 in (46 x 46 x 61 cm)</td><td>4.5 cu ft</td><td>Bedding, towels, pillows, lampshades</td></tr><tr><td>Extra-large</td><td>24 x 18 x 24 in (61 x 46 x 61 cm)</td><td>6 cu ft</td><td>Comforters, cushions, light bulky items</td></tr><tr><td>Wardrobe</td><td>About 24 in (61 cm) wide</td><td>Varies</td><td>Clothes on hangers</td></tr><tr><td>Dish pack</td><td>18 x 18 x 28 in (46 x 46 x 71 cm)</td><td>5.25 cu ft</td><td>Plates, glasses, china</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The sizes come from <a href="https://www.uhaul.com/MovingSupplies/Boxes/Standard-Sized-Moving-Boxes/Small-Moving-Box?id=3245" target="_blank" rel="noopener">U-Haul</a>, which rates its small box for up to 65 lb and recommends it for books, tools and canned food. Its double-walled <a href="https://www.uhaul.com/MovingSupplies/Boxes/Double-Wall-Boxes/Dish-Barrel-Box?id=2573" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Dish Barrel box</a> measures 18 x 18 x 28 in and is made for dishes, glassware and other fragile items, with a divider kit sold separately. Other stores sell slightly different sizes, so compare the dimensions rather than the names.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img decoding="async" width="1024" height="1024" src="https://dailyspacehacks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/moving-box-calculator-02-box-sizes.jpg" alt="Four sealed cardboard moving boxes lined up from small to extra-large on a wood floor, with flat boxes leaning against the wall" class="wp-image-2335" srcset="https://dailyspacehacks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/moving-box-calculator-02-box-sizes.jpg 1024w, https://dailyspacehacks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/moving-box-calculator-02-box-sizes-300x300.jpg 300w, https://dailyspacehacks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/moving-box-calculator-02-box-sizes-150x150.jpg 150w, https://dailyspacehacks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/moving-box-calculator-02-box-sizes-768x768.jpg 768w" sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading">How Many Boxes per Room</h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Every room packs differently. Kitchens fill the most boxes for their size because of dishes, glasses and pantry food, while bathrooms need only a few. These are the average counts the moving box calculator uses before adjusting for how much you own:</p>



<figure class="wp-block-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Room</th><th>Small</th><th>Medium</th><th>Large and XL</th><th>Specialty</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Main bedroom</td><td>3</td><td>4</td><td>4</td><td>2 wardrobe boxes</td></tr><tr><td>Other bedroom</td><td>2</td><td>3</td><td>3</td><td>1 wardrobe box</td></tr><tr><td>Living room</td><td>3</td><td>4</td><td>4</td><td>–</td></tr><tr><td>Kitchen (2 bedrooms)</td><td>5</td><td>5</td><td>2</td><td>2 dish packs</td></tr><tr><td>Dining room</td><td>2</td><td>2</td><td>1</td><td>1 dish pack</td></tr><tr><td>Bathroom</td><td>2</td><td>1</td><td>–</td><td>–</td></tr><tr><td>Home office</td><td>4</td><td>3</td><td>1</td><td>–</td></tr><tr><td>Garage, basement or attic</td><td>3</td><td>4</td><td>6</td><td>–</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">For hanging clothes, <a href="https://www.movingplace.com/moving-advice/how-many-moving-boxes-do-i-need" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Moving Place</a> suggests about one wardrobe box for every 2 feet (60 cm) of closet rail, and one or two dish packs per kitchen. If your garage, basement or attic is full, count it as two rooms. Our <a href="https://dailyspacehacks.com/how-to-declutter-your-home/">guide to decluttering your home</a> helps you cut the pile before you pack.</p>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Packing Supplies Checklist</h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Boxes are only half the shopping list. Buy these at the same time so packing day does not stop halfway:</p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><strong>Packing tape.</strong> Wide 2 in (48 mm) tape and a tape gun. Plan on roughly one roll for every 15 boxes, because each box needs tape across the bottom and top seams.</li>


<li><strong>Packing paper.</strong> Plain newsprint for wrapping dishes and glasses. Newspaper ink can rub off on plates.</li>


<li><strong>Bubble wrap.</strong> One roll for lamps, frames, mirrors and electronics.</li>


<li><strong>Markers and labels.</strong> Write the room and a short list of contents on two sides of every box, not the top, so you can read them when boxes are stacked.</li>


<li><strong>Furniture pads or blankets.</strong> To protect furniture, mirrors and floors on moving day.</li>
</ul>



